-- Row 99 wave 2 deleted `until`. This fixture was `pattern_until.vlt` and
-- asserted `VLT0107`, and the re-point is §2.3's third disposition: the program
-- is still wrong, for a different reason, and §2.3 warns that a fixture which
-- still fails with an unexamined `.stderr` has stopped testing what it was
-- written to test. So the reason is written down rather than inherited.
--
-- What it used to assert: `until c` lowered to `while !(c)`, and a pattern test
-- cannot be negated — `while !(let Some(v) = x)` is not Rust. The nearest Rust
-- that compiles, `while !matches!(x, Some(_))`, binds nothing, so it cannot be
-- what a binding construct meant, and lowering to it would be doc 02 §5.2's
-- failure mode. Plan 22 §1.3 reported instead.
--
-- That asymmetry is why the keyword is gone. `until` declined a pattern test
-- while `while` accepts one, so the keyword meant as sugar for `while` could do
-- strictly less than it — and `VLT0107` existed only to say so. Both are retired
-- together.
main : ()
main =
  until .pop queue is Some v
    println! \-> "#{v}"
